TITLE: Policy reference
SUMMARY: A policy says which workloads Pahlevan governs, and what the kernel does with
an operation that falls outside what it learned.
HEADINGS:
  #headings-and-emphasis Headings and emphasis
  #a-fenced-code-block A fenced code block
  #a-table A table
  #lists Lists
ASSETS: 
BODY:
<h2 id="headings-and-emphasis">Headings and emphasis</h2>
<h3 id="a-third-level-heading">A third-level heading</h3>
<p>Text with <strong>bold</strong>, <em>italic</em>, <code>inline code</code>, and a <a href="architecture.html">link to another doc</a>,
a <a href="quick-start.html#installation">link with a fragment</a>, an <a href="https://example.org/x" target="_blank" rel="noopener">external link</a>,
a <a href="../changelog.html">link to a repository file</a>, and a <a href="https://github.com/obsernetics/pahlevan/blob/main/Makefile" target="_blank" rel="noopener">link to a file with no page</a>.</p>
<h2 id="a-fenced-code-block">A fenced code block</h2>
<pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: policy.pahlevan.io/v1alpha1
kind: PahlevanPolicy
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: web
</code></pre>
<pre><code>no language on this fence
</code></pre>
<h2 id="a-table">A table</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Field</th>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Required</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>selector</code></td>
<td><code>LabelSelector</code></td>
<td>yes</td>
<td>Which workloads the policy governs</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>mode</code></td>
<td>string</td>
<td>no</td>
<td><code>monitor</code> or <code>enforce</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
